### 🐛 What happened?

Title: Desktop App 2.1.57 crashes with React error #185 (Maximum update depth exceeded) in scroll overflow hook

## Environment
- App: LobeHub Desktop `2.1.57`
- OS: macOS
- Date observed: `2026-05-11`
- Error:
  - `Minified React error #185`
  - Full message: `Maximum update depth exceeded`

## Stack trace (key part)
- `dispatchSetState`
- `checkScroll`
- `commitHookEffectListMount`
- `commitPassiveMountOnFiber`

(From runtime bundle: `app://renderer/assets/es-DynfgelQ.js` and `client-Bh6kKd0F.js`)

## What seems to happen (inferred from bundle code)
A scroll overflow hook appears to:
1. call `checkScroll()` inside `useEffect`
2. unconditionally call `setScrollState(newState)`
3. include unstable deps such as `onVisibilityChange`/`updateDeps`

This can create:
`effect -> setState -> render -> effect` loop, causing React #185.

## Suggested fix
- Guard state updates: only update if value actually changed.
- Keep callback in `ref` to avoid effect re-running due to callback identity changes.
- Trigger `onVisibilityChange` only when state changed.

## Proposed patch (concept)
```ts
const isSame = (a: ScrollState, b: ScrollState) =>
  a.top === b.top && a.bottom === b.bottom && a.left === b.left && a.right === b.right;

const onVisibilityChangeRef = useRef(onVisibilityChange);
useEffect(() => {
  onVisibilityChangeRef.current = onVisibilityChange;
}, [onVisibilityChange]);

useEffect(() => {
  const element = domRef.current;
  if (!element || !isEnabled) return;

  const checkScroll = () => {
    const next = calcScrollState(element, orientation, offset);

    setScrollState((prev) => {
      if (isSame(prev, next)) return prev;
      onVisibilityChangeRef.current?.(next);
      return next;
    });
  };

  checkScroll();
  element.addEventListener('scroll', checkScroll);
  window.addEventListener('resize', checkScroll);
  const ro = new ResizeObserver(checkScroll);
  ro.observe(element);

  return () => {
    element.removeEventListener('scroll', checkScroll);
    window.removeEventListener('resize', checkScroll);
    ro.disconnect();
  };
}, [domRef, offset, orientation, isEnabled, ...updateDeps]);


